# Beancount files mean what their line endings say: like bean-check, a lone
# "*" or ":" line is skipped before CRLF but a syntax error before LF. Keep
# them LF on every checkout, Windows included, so the fixtures test the same
# input everywhere.
*.beancount text eol=lf
# Fixtures named crlf_* test CRLF line endings: keep their bytes as written.
crlf_*.beancount -text
